WEBVTT

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.751
<v><b>Tim:</b></v> Um, I think to an extent you are always going to be influenced

00:00:13.761 --> 00:00:15.776
by the way you were brought up yourself.

00:00:21.703 --> 00:00:26.477
<v><b>Tim:</b></v> Um, for example, my younger children are part of the digital age,

00:00:26.886 --> 00:00:31.739
and so it’s always a little bit of a tussle, a fight with them, to get them off screens.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:42.139
<v><b>Tim:</b></v> And with my 27-year-old and my 29-year-old, there were screens,

00:00:42.158 --> 00:00:44.695
but they weren’t that interesting and they weren’t on

00:00:44.718 --> 00:00:46.641
– they didn’t want to be on them the whole time.

00:00:52.087 --> 00:00:54.587
<v><b>Syinat:</b></v> Well, so, for example, my mother, when we were growing up,

00:00:54.612 --> 00:00:59.626
she always tried to make me see us as equals in, in the relationship and so,

00:00:59.864 --> 00:01:02.606
I definitely plan on doing that with my children as well.

00:01:08.307 --> 00:01:11.874
<v><b>Syinat:</b></v> …and so, I definitely plan on doing that with my children as well…

00:01:11.928 --> 00:01:13.705
even if that is more of a positive thing.

00:01:19.462 --> 00:01:24.949
<v><b>Devika:</b></v> So, myself and, um, people of my generation were brought up in quite strict households…

00:01:30.821 --> 00:01:32.927
<v><b>Devika:</b></v> …and it’s been interesting, actually, to see, for example,

00:01:32.952 --> 00:01:36.085
one of my cousins is bringing up their children in a very different way, …